//! task: fix
//! ask: Write a function that doubles its argument through a local named `per`.
//! expect: EXS-E0201,EXS-E0220,EXS-E0303
//! primary: EXS-E0220
//! refs: §8.4
//! explain: `per` is one of the thirty reserved words and can never be an identifier, anywhere. The reserved words read as plausible variable names, which is why `EXS-E0220` has a code of its own and `exsc` attaches a suggested edit (`per` to `per_`). The other two codes are recovery cascade from the same line. Contextual words (`versio`, `lt`, `maior`, ...) are different: they remain legal names outside their position.

publica functio duplica(a: u64) -> u64 {
    firma per: u64 = a * 2;
    redde per;
}
//@ fixed
publica functio duplica(a: u64) -> u64 {
    firma per_: u64 = a * 2;
    redde per_;
}
